<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:43:13Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany news: Merz urges CDU discipline as pressure grows</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a9d64ed94cd3e9c761f1b346778636763ff4e30193e20ba9b4dda1459faefa13</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T00:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-urges-cdu-discipline-as-pressure-grows/live-79256902--10c6578e951f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-urges-cdu-discipline-as-pressure-grows/live-79256902?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz has urged his party to stay disciplined as pressure grows over his leadership. Meanwhile, Germany's homeownership rate has fallen to its lowest level in 20 years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Berlin businesswoman charged with spying for Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ace196c51b400d47718e311034f5bd230160ba3b41c7883f21bab816fe8ea4e8</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T11:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/berlin-businesswoman-charged-with-spying-for-russia/a-79258004--e5381277f598.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/berlin-businesswoman-charged-with-spying-for-russia/a-79258004?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prosecutors say the Berlin marketing executive used her political and military contacts to help a Russian intelligence officer gain access to influential circles and seek information on German defense policy.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Merz's CDU comes out on top in Lower Saxony polls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ce3001a3077799b48b00593f8e1b9d729d78f02438fead8db212fcf506b60cb</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T06:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-merz-s-cdu-comes-out-on-top-in-lower-saxony-polls/a-79254724--04c4d8ef8565.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-merz-s-cdu-comes-out-on-top-in-lower-saxony-polls/a-79254724?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Christian Democrats have emerged as the strongest party following local elections in the state of Lower Saxony. The vote was closely watched as an indicator of the strength of the far-right AfD, which came in third.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Zverev wins US Open in golden year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6249b34648d5e0d6b92e96693b7235a86d923e34517cb400e4a28816dae68ad0</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T22:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-zverev-wins-us-open-in-golden-year/a-79212706--d962ccd6a0c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-zverev-wins-us-open-in-golden-year/a-79212706?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Alexander Zverev has won the US Open for the first time, defeating Ben Shelton in the final. It is Zverev's second Grand Slam win of 2026 after a long wait for his first title, but controversy still hangs over him.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Berlin election driven by radical ideas</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:505df8f5d45f6f88ff7cb1a54a90a0c4135b48bc436acc52efbc3488abad69e4</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T11:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/berlin-election-driven-by-radical-ideas/a-79256516--15d2b53f017a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/berlin-election-driven-by-radical-ideas/a-79256516?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The results of the Berlin election are as hard to predict as ever. Three parties are vying for first place, including the socialist Left Party and the far-right AfD. But one issue is most important to Berliners.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>SPD governor campaigns as one-woman bulwark against AfD</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d1d22c067a344c2f452e3bba6dd30958c3ccda317151339357ce9cecbfed770</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T11:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spd-governor-campaigns-as-one-woman-bulwark-against-afd/a-79264225--0135376188de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spd-governor-campaigns-as-one-woman-bulwark-against-afd/a-79264225?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Manuela Schwesig, of the center-left SPD, has governed the state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania, on the Baltic Sea coast, since 2017. Ahead of this weekend's election, she is campaigning against the nationalist AfD.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Women's Basketball World Cup: Can Germany harness a boom?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4631c5cadfe6289f9ba37643bb13348b1ca2a4f12990572fd7b4a71f283b2e0c</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T15:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-basketball-world-cup-can-germany-harness-a-boom/a-79263602--77d972e02866.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-basketball-world-cup-can-germany-harness-a-boom/a-79263602?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany thrilled fans at the Women's Basketball World Cup. But even if this sparked a boom in the women's game, the infrastructure simply isn't ready for it.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Far-right AfD puts pressure on German aid to Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:290e2e045d8c3471e64a8091918b24fe631caff2d80105ccc5b91f1efc341025</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:43:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/far-right-afd-puts-pressure-on-german-aid-to-ukraine/a-79257524--80d6e129ea25.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/far-right-afd-puts-pressure-on-german-aid-to-ukraine/a-79257524?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Emboldened by its win in Saxony-Anhalt, the far-right Alternative for Germany wants the government to change its Ukraine and Russia policies. Berlin is staying the course, but support is fading — especially in the east.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>In cosmopolitan Berlin, elections still closed to foreigners</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f17de51251260307333575376a4c495404ddbc6714bae64e99dd8fdb83f844d</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T07:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-cosmopolitan-berlin-elections-still-closed-to-foreigners/a-78744579--2c7a3b66c58f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-cosmopolitan-berlin-elections-still-closed-to-foreigners/a-78744579?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A quarter of Berlin residents will have no say in the German capital's city-state election because they lack citizenship. That's the highest proportion of residents excluded from the election yet, and many are unhappy.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Elversberg: Bundesliga newcomers from tiny town make waves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e1008e513888d9b989db3dbc70cc7058483d779cfedd92bb0f166d4c67592fe</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483--9d72d35ebb6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A team from a small southwestern German town of just 7,000 inhabitants made history by sealing promotion to become the 59th club to play in the Bundesliga. Elversberg has got off to a memorable start.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Werner Herzog: Germany's wild man of cinema is back</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9fdb2404e0224d54167320cc5adda56cdfad936ca6f8aa9bc66f64c0cee64c7</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324--4a5372e58812.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As his latest movie, "Bucking Fastard," premiered at the Venice Film Festival, DW talked to the boundary-breaking director.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
